# Commit message after each change

The user commits themselves. Whenever you finish a batch of code/test/rule changes (not mid-exploration), end with a **short commit subject** they can paste.

## Format

- One line, ~50–72 characters when practical
- Imperative mood (“Fix…”, “Add…”, “Block…”)
- Focus on **why**, not a file list
- No trailing period
- Optional: a second line blank then 1–2 short body lines only if needed

## Example

```text
Suggested commit message:
Block empty check-in; use Undo Checkout for unchanged locks
```

Do **not** run `git commit` unless they explicitly ask. Still give the message text even when they only asked for the fix.
